Hmm, that's different to my experience with nethack on Mac OS X (I
don't use tiles, mind. Maybe you should try it without tiles and see if
it's the same); it works similar to nethack on windows for me - asks my
name, and keeps my character as that name (you can rename your save
files to rename your characters), (unless I'm starting in wizard mode,
when it calls you Wizard regardless, though you can then rename it).

As for editing your settings, there should be a file in the same folder
as nethack called Nethack Defaults, which you can then open in
whichever text editor you please, and continue as you would.



